{"id":"u-87ebd4ba-01af-4836-8b1a-f771c6ca95e0","src":"community","title":"Fireground Readiness","author":"Ian Sherer","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/x81YuQ-fireground-built","desc":"Fireground Readiness is a 12-week firefighter performance system designed to build real-world strength, power, and sustained work capacity under fatigue. It prepares firefighters to perform demanding physical tasks while wearing gear, managing unpredictable conditions, and maintaining output across long shifts.\n\nOne of the key focal points of the program is maximizing conditioning efficiency and oxygen utilization under load. Conditioning sessions are structured to improve aerobic capacity, recovery between efforts, and the ability to sustain performance while managing breathing under fatigue.\n\nThe program is also designed to be highly adaptable to the environment. All training can be completed in a firehouse, commercial gym, or basic training space with minimal equipment requirements. This ensures consistency regardless of schedule, station assignment, or facility access.\n\nWeekly Training Split\n\nDay 1: Lower Body + Power\nDay 2: Modality (Incline walk, Stair stepper, bike, etc.)\nDay 3: Upper\nDay 4: Intervals\nDay 5: Fireground Circuit\nDay 6: Long Slow Duration Run\n\nProgression Structure\n\nThe program runs for 12 weeks and is split into three phases.\n\nFoundation: Weeks 1-4\nBuild movement quality, aerobic base, and foundational strength. Intensity stays around RPE 5-7.\n\nBuild: Weeks 5-8\nDevelops strength under fatigue and improves work capacity through heavier lifting and structured conditioning. Intensity stays around RPE 7-8.\n\nPeak: Weeks 9-12\nMaximizes strength, power, and conditioning output under fatigue. Week 12 tapers to consolidate performance. Intensity stays around RPE 8-9.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced","Beginner"],"goals":["Bodyweight Fitness","Strength","Muscle","Athletics"],"equipment":["Dumbbell Only"],"minutes":60,"joins":11,"rate":0,"ra